## Security gates (frozen)

- No outbound fetch without egress allowlist (EG-01 before PSP-01)
- Webhook HMAC + ±5m timestamp + replay cache
- Secrets in env only — never in workspace metadata JSON
- Stripe new code uses **Accounts v2** API

---

## Threat model (frozen — P5-D-N-001 DOC-D-01)

P5-D restores legacy integration seams **without** re-opening SSRF, replay, or secret-leak paths documented in [`legacy-vs-denali-gap-analysis.md`](../../apps/api/docs/legacy-vs-denali-gap-analysis.md) § Proxy & Third-Party Integration Gap.

### Assets

| Asset | Why it matters |
|-------|----------------|
| Platform egress credentials | Zibal merchant key, Stripe secret key — full PSP authority |
| Tenant-scoped callback URLs | Stored on club config; attacker-controlled if validation weak |
| Inbound webhook bodies | Forged events could mark registrations paid without PSP proof |
| Operator/admin session | Can trigger outbound PSP calls via future finance routes |

### Adversaries & goals

| Actor | Goal | Primary control |
|-------|------|-----------------|
| Tenant operator (malicious) | SSRF via callback URL or map/geocode proxy | EG-01 `assertSafeOutboundUrl` before any tenant-influenced URL fetch |
| External attacker | Replay signed webhook | WH-01 HMAC + ±5m skew + replay cache (WH-02) |
| External attacker | Forge webhook without secret | HMAC verify fail-closed; no side effects on bad signature |
| Compromised metadata JSON | Exfiltrate PSP secrets via workspace definition publish | Secrets **never** in metadata — env / platform vault only (F4 from epic spec) |

### Trust boundaries

```text
[Browser] → [apps/web BFF] → [apps/api operator routes]
                                    ↓ (tenant-scoped, authenticated)
                              [TenantHttpProxy + egress-url]
                                    ↓ (allowlisted hosts only)
                              [Zibal / Stripe / Resend / MinIO]

[PSP] → POST /internal/payments/webhook → signature guard → idempotent handler
```

**Denali frozen:** offline receipt clubs never traverse PSP egress in P5-D v1 — gateway activation remains blocked by P5-C GU-02 until P5-D-N-010 lifts the guard.

### Outbound egress sequence (frozen — P5-D-N-001 DOC-D-02)

Every outbound HTTP call from tenant-influenced input follows this order — **no step may be skipped**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Caller as API handler
  participant Guard as assertSafeOutboundUrl
  participant Proxy as TenantHttpProxy
  participant PSP as Allowlisted upstream

  Caller->>Guard: parse URL (protocol, host, port)
  alt private IP / metadata / link-local / bad protocol
    Guard-->>Caller: throw EGRESS_URL_BLOCKED
  else host ∉ allowlist
    Guard-->>Caller: throw EGRESS_HOST_NOT_ALLOWLISTED
  else allowed
    Guard->>Proxy: fetchWithPinnedEgress(url, signal)
    Proxy->>PSP: TLS connect (pinned DNS, rejectUnauthorized)
    PSP-->>Proxy: response
    Proxy-->>Caller: bounded body + status
  end
```

Implementation targets (N-002..N-003):

| Step | Owner | Assert |
|------|-------|--------|
| URL guard | `apps/api/src/integrations/egress/` | EG-01 blocks `127.0.0.1`; EG-02 blocks metadata IP host |
| Proxy wire | `tenant-http-proxy.ts` + `main.ts` bootstrap | All map/finance outbound uses proxy — no raw global `fetch` |
| Timeout | Proxy `AbortSignal` | PI-01 — no unbounded hang |

