## Payments webhook ingress (frozen — P5-D-N-006 WH-01)

Implementation: `apps/api/src/integrations/webhooks/`

Route: `POST /internal/payments/webhook`

| Assert | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| WH-01 | HMAC-SHA256 over `${timestamp}.${rawBody}` with `PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET` |
| WH-01b | `x-payments-webhook-signature` + `x-payments-webhook-timestamp` required — missing → 401 |
| WH-01c | Timestamp skew ±5 minutes — outside window → 401 |
| WH-01d | Bad signature → 401; handler not invoked (fail-closed) |
| WH-01e | Optional `PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_ALLOWED_IPS` comma list — mismatch → 403 |

Replay cache (WH-02) — see N-007 section below. Finance side effects deferred to P5-E.

Spec: `apps/api/test/payments-webhook-signature.spec.ts`.

---

## Payments webhook replay cache (frozen — P5-D-N-007 WH-02)

Implementation: `apps/api/src/integrations/webhooks/payments-webhook-replay-cache.ts`

| Assert | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| WH-02 | `claimPaymentsWebhookEvent(eventId)` returns `fresh` on first sighting within TTL |
| WH-02b | Duplicate `eventId` within TTL → route returns HTTP 200 noop (`replayed: true`, `accepted: false`) |
| WH-02c | After TTL expiry, same `eventId` may be claimed `fresh` again |
| WH-02d | Signed webhook without resolvable `eventId` → 400 `PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_EVENT_ID_REQUIRED` |

**Env:** `PAYMENTS_WEBHOOK_REPLAY_TTL_SEC` (optional; default 24h).

Spec: `apps/api/test/payments-webhook-replay.spec.ts`.

